    Instances come out of `Reduction.terms`; there is no public constructor.

    ## Examples
    ```python
    _, master = oneloop.reduce(family, [1, 1]).terms[0]

    master.kind
    # 'bubble'

    master.arguments
    # [s, 0, 0]

    master.to_expression()
    # oneloopmaster::B0(s,0,0,1)
    ```
    """
